        { q:"Why did Alma call Corianton's sin so serious?", choices:["It damaged his health","It cost the family money","It gave unbelievers a reason to deny the faith","It broke the yearly feast"], a:2, why:"Alma said Corianton's wicked example kept people from believing his words and destroyed their confidence in the church." },
        { q:"What did Alma tell Corianton to do?", choices:["Return to the ministry with his brothers after repenting","Become chief judge","Stay home in Zarahemla permanently","Lead the armies at Manti"], a:0, why:"Alma commanded him to repent, then go and declare the word with his brothers Shiblon and Helaman." }
